akantu-rs oracle patch 0002 — embedded: fix DECLARE_NAMED_ARGUMENT arity

Upstream: akantu 35a851780d0b9471d258ed53a003ae98aaa95ea0, src/model/model_options.hh
Bug: introduced by upstream commit ad98b0167 (2024-10-15, "allows
solver_options in initFull"): inside `#ifdef AKANTU_EMBEDDED` the one-argument
macro DECLARE_NAMED_ARGUMENT(name) is called with two arguments, so every
translation unit that includes model_options.hh fails to compile whenever the
`embedded` package is enabled (upstream CI never enables it).
Fix: declare the named argument `init_intersections` (the only name used by
EmbeddedInterfaceModelOptions' named-argument constructor). No behaviour
change for builds without `embedded`.
NOT APPLIED: embedded stays OFF (material_reinforcement is unfinished
upstream WIP); kept as a documented candidate fix. See docs/DECISIONS.md
(D-032), docs/BLOCKERS.md (B-003).

--- a/src/model/model_options.hh	2026-11-09 16:57:03
+++ b/src/model/model_options.hh	2026-11-09 16:57:03
@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@
 #ifdef AKANTU_EMBEDDED
 
 namespace {
-  DECLARE_NAMED_ARGUMENT(init_intersections, non_linear_solver);
+  DECLARE_NAMED_ARGUMENT(init_intersections);
 }
 /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
 struct EmbeddedInterfaceModelOptions : SolidMechanicsModelOptions {
